{"question": "A florist has 144 roses. she arranges them into bouquets, each containing 9 roses. if she sells 8 full bouquets and uses the rest to decorate her shop, how many roses did she use for decoration?", "raw_instances": "Let's break down the problem step by step:\n\n1. **Total roses:**  \n   The florist has 144 roses.\n\n2. **Roses per bouquet:**  \n   Each bouquet contains 9 roses.\n\n3. **Bouquets sold:**  \n   She sells 8 full bouquets.\n\n4. **Calculate roses used in bouquets:**  \n   \\( 8 \\text{ bouquets} \\times 9 \\text{ roses/bouquet} = 72 \\text{ roses} \\)\n\n5. **Calculate remaining roses for decoration:**  \n   \\( 144 \\text{ total roses} - 72 \\text{ roses in bouquets} = 72 \\text{ roses} \\)\n\n**Result:**\n72", "most_similar": {"A baker made 120 cookies for a school event. she packed them into boxes, with each box holding 8 cookies. if she gave away 3 full boxes to the teachers and kept the rest for the students, how many cookies did the students get?": 0.35000000000000003, "A farmer harvested 360 apples from his orchard. he placed them into baskets, each holding 12 apples. if he sold 5 full baskets at the market and kept the rest for making cider, how many apples did he keep for cider?": 0.33766233766233766, "Mrs. Jackson has four boxes of Christmas decorations. There are 15 decorations in each box. She was only able to use 35 decorations and decided to give the rest to her neighbor. How many decorations did she give?": 0.3243243243243243, "A library has 150 books. each shelf can hold 10 books. if the librarian fills 8 shelves and donates the rest of the books to a school, how many books does the school receive?": 0.31428571428571433, "Jean has 60 stuffies.  She keeps 1/3 of them and then gives away the rest.  She gives 1/4 of what she gave away to her sister Janet.  How many stuffies did Janet get?": 0.3098591549295775, "Maria has 19 cookies. She decided to give her friend 5 of them, and half of the rest to her family. From the rest, Mari